  "adaptations": [
    "The measured three-oscillator, dual-filter, mixer, amplifier, macro and modulation/FX/analyzer panel geometry follows the supplied concept. This is a native vector implementation, not the reference bitmap.",
    "The shared header replaces decorative OS chrome and concept navigation with working preset navigation, scene selection, skin selection, full-editor access and a real master-volume control.",
    "Oscillator algorithms and parameter names are always supplied by Surge. The concept's generic Sample mode is not fabricated; unused algorithm parameters are disabled.",
    "The right envelope is the actual filter envelope, while the amplifier panel exposes the actual amplitude envelope. Surge has two envelope generators rather than four concept EG tabs.",
    "Per-filter envelope depth replaces the concept's independent drive knobs. The actual shared waveshaper drive remains available in the routing strip.",
    "The routing diagram is a schematic of supported native modes, not a general-purpose modular patcher. All controls use native parameter IDs.",
    "The first eight FX algorithms and six current slot-1 parameters are shown; the full editor retains all sixteen FX slots and every effect parameter.",
    "Live output meters and the native scope action replace fabricated spectrum activity. Oscillator and envelope graphics reflect current state rather than baked image traces.",
    "A compact bottom utility strip adds real scene and voice controls in the concept's otherwise unused lower margin. Full original editor, advanced modulation and preset workflows remain available.",
    "The compact oscillator tuning readouts and stacked right-envelope A/D/S/R fields are live, draggable and unit-aware numeric controls. Macro knob centres have been aligned to the concept's two measured rows."
  ]
}
